      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lake Hart, a 1,881‑acre freshwater lake, gave the community its name but is a Class III impaired water body due to historic lead and mercury in fish.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
